represent the level curves of the surface $z=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y$ shown above?" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363965 1113 #uuid "9ec437fa-7d05-53d2-8259-19727f28f519" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363965 1145 "First, notice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $[-1,1].$ So, we will consider only $c$-level curves for $c\\in [-1,1].$\n\nThe level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & =c \\\\ y & =-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡c+2\\pi n,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ can be any integer. \n\nNotice that the equations $y=-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡c+2\\pi n$ do not depend on $x.$ So, for a given $c\\in [-1,1]$ and integer $n$, the right-hand side of the equation is constant. As a result, we obtain a family of horizontal lines, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/67e9cfee7779fdde389a0804e7f52372ca9434de56b6611d296d4ac9c0759f72.png)" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363966 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363967 13194139535735 true] [17592186363966 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363968 13194139535735 true] [17592186363966 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363969 13194139535735 true] [17592186363966 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363970 13194139535735 true] [17592186363966 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363971 13194139535735 true] [17592186363966 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535735 true] [17592186363966 1041 "selection" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363966 1104 #edb/ref 17592186363969 13194139535735 true] [17592186363966 1110 #uuid "7bd5fd88-c341-5d33-a06a-b249288d207d" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363967 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/56e923e4c1e2603c9bd3c621df0a5a4043fcc6a37ac73427be14541407fc19d8.png" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363967 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535735 true] [17592186363967 1111 #uuid "93cb7e55-2150-5080-9903-922ca34c9007" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363968 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/bf0f4b592cde648f63b21523aba1a49aeeb3b4dcaf909ba72c4629e088ca372a.png" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363968 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535735 true] [17592186363968 1111 #uuid "d5fac066-b7e1-5b1a-92c8-18b880099c2a" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363969 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/67e9cfee7779fdde389a0804e7f52372ca9434de56b6611d296d4ac9c0759f72.png" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363969 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535735 true] [17592186363969 1111 #uuid "efe2f36b-4e61-58a3-9d0a-e8f44ae8a871" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363970 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/09f1a18e1a6fdcd29a40026cbffd8e8bdec23511bb692a1e920c18f942042470.png" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363970 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535735 true] [17592186363970 1111 #uuid "d9862cec-d2cf-5bea-9a7f-abe4dd0acc4d" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363971 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/aa4d0cd189808c717648640c5543a632c099970a19d38d44298d409054f2627c.png" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363971 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535735 true] [17592186363971 1111 #uuid "d5c71f78-d19f-5a27-81e3-6db69cacd8b4" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363972 1017 #edb/ref 17592186363973 13194139535735 true] [17592186363972 1089 "q-129118" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363972 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535735 true] [17592186363972 1100 "Which of the following represents the level curves of $f(x,y)=-x-y+2?$" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363972 1113 #uuid "fdd99af4-5961-5150-ae64-8efce48fac73" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363972 1145 "The level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nnotice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider $c$-level curves for any real value of $c.$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ -x-y+2 & =c \\\\ y & =-x+2-c.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of lines with slope of $-1.$ Therefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/e20175ef9ac473a621a67d524e60cacc6e9a40ba30267fe81b4e6a093c780c28.png)" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363973 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363974 13194139535735 true] [17592186363973 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363975 13194139535735 true] [17592186363973 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363976 13194139535735 true] [17592186363973 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363977 13194139535735 true] [17592186363973 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363978 13194139535735 true] [17592186363973 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535735 true] [17592186363973 1041 "selection" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363973 1104 #edb/ref 17592186363974 13194139535735 true] [17592186363973 1110 #uuid "7cdebb0d-3dd1-5854-a760-38aa8a17c565" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363974 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/7afff53b46a661fc6e0df4df871810dc5514ff7b476294e76c70f60d4e1643f9.png" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363974 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535735 true] [17592186363974 1111 #uuid "4cb84bfe-c871-5320-9d4c-83f92579b07b" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363975 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/b79c75fb4de77313ff9ae17938eeabc8b55cca395e6516c09abf6742f9b6a23b.png" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363975 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535735 true] [17592186363975 1111 #uuid "c637bc28-4d05-5ed2-b6b9-1edf81fd13a3" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363976 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/0162f31b5dbb35c6d370dff9b54257708df39b6957f6547059842cd31769669b.png" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363976 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535735 true] [17592186363976 1111 #uuid "dc098fa2-da6b-5025-8d8d-4e55c6bae734" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363977 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/b4642ea9b585ac066f2ed904b1bee4df7d1ff3449ba2d09afca8364b58f1dcba.png" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363977 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535735 true] [17592186363977 1111 #uuid "bff51616-e5c0-5d20-abc4-71ea33277efb" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363978 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/f82efe38e48f39aee18cf9e00cdd69f07c37cc414b08b5bc78ebc0a876c02d7e.png" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363978 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535735 true] [17592186363978 1111 #uuid "e067a96f-7163-5e68-ac5f-5ac9b0900d8f" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363979 1017 #edb/ref 17592186363980 13194139535735 true] [17592186363979 1089 "q-35527" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363979 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535735 true] [17592186363979 1100 "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=xy$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $c=1$ gives a hyperbola\n- $c=-1$ gives a parabola\n- $c=0$ gives the axes $x=0$ and $y=0$" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363979 1113 #uuid "fb8b2d04-67d4-51d3-8ebf-71fc804b1a61" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363979 1145 "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}xy & =c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=\\pm 1$ then the level curves are $xy=\\pm 1,$ which are hyperbolas.\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curves are $xy=0,$ which consists of the axes $x=0$ and $y=0.$\n\nSo, only statements I and III are true." 13194139535735 true] [17592186363980 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363981 13194139535735 true] [17592186363980 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363982 13194139535735 true] [17592186363980 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363983 13194139535735 true] [17592186363980 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363984 13194139535735 true] [17592186363980 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363985 13194139535735 true] [17592186363980 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535735 true] [17592186363980 1041 "selection" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363980 1104 #edb/ref 17592186363982 13194139535735 true] [17592186363980 1110 #uuid "375cdb08-607e-5f82-98dc-008ebfc21d03" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363981 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363981 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535735 true] [17592186363981 1111 #uuid "063c3081-fc99-5c59-9c9c-17dc1247f778" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363982 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363982 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535735 true] [17592186363982 1111 #uuid "e6de069c-00e7-55c3-abef-12f93304c62a" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363983 1034 "I only" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363983 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535735 true] [17592186363983 1111 #uuid "93ab8cf8-df3c-545b-9e70-4de71e0b453c" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363984 1034 "III only" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363984 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535735 true] [17592186363984 1111 #uuid "40169a3d-04d9-5678-84cf-d8a54ff12072" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363985 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363985 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535735 true] [17592186363985 1111 #uuid "b0e38b30-9540-5800-a818-37d8d43cae7c" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363986 1017 #edb/ref 17592186363987 13194139535735 true] [17592186363986 1089 "q-71395" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363986 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535735 true] [17592186363986 1100 "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $c=1$ gives a line\n- $c=2$ gives a hyperbola\n- $c=0$ gives two lines" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363986 1113 #uuid "8f4b2eba-eaa0-5faa-a68a-66c51bc54701" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363986 1145 "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}} & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}-2{y}^{2} & ={c}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=1$ then the level curve is ${x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}=1,$ which is not a line.\n\n- If $c=2$ then the level curve is ${x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}=4,$ which is a hyperbola.\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curve is $y=\\pm \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{2}},$ which consists of two lines.\n\nSo, only statements II and III are true." 13194139535735 true] [17592186363987 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363988 13194139535735 true] [17592186363987 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363989 13194139535735 true] [17592186363987 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363990 13194139535735 true] [17592186363987 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363991 13194139535735 true] [17592186363987 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363992 13194139535735 true] [17592186363987 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535735 true] [17592186363987 1041 "selection" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363987 1104 #edb/ref 17592186363988 13194139535735 true] [17592186363987 1110 #uuid "ba0d035f-188d-5d33-9360-40e5e980a843" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363988 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363988 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535735 true] [17592186363988 1111 #uuid "286957ec-8684-5aae-8c65-4489a40574c4" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363989 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363989 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535735 true] [17592186363989 1111 #uuid "8fe6c2e5-9236-5ba4-93ec-d695c3eb9c67" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363990 1034 "I only" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363990 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535735 true] [17592186363990 1111 #uuid "97dcfe1e-2ae5-5418-bd47-555110b4615c" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363991 1034 "III only" 13194139535735 true] [17592186363991 1103 #edb/ref 175